  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the highest-priority need is to establish a performance baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most standard configuration in the search space: a single modality, single profile, and the most conventional linear encoder (PCA). It will (1) calibrate what accuracy/F1 levels are achievable in this task, (2) serve as the reference against which all other RNA encoder choices (scvi, scgpt), profile settings (multiprofile + aggregation), and the addition of image modality can be measured, and (3) is computationally inexpensive, reducing the cost of the first data point. Establishing this floor first ensures that every subsequent experiment—whether testing a richer RNA encoder, adding image features, or trying multimodal fusion—can be interpreted as a meaningful delta rather than an absolute number in isolation. This is the most information-efficient use of the first budget slot."
}

